"""Saltmarsh: a hover raid on the Iver Delta, 2187.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine, with the engine's optional rules for fast mechanized
warfare: ranged fire, a second movement phase after combat, disabled
results, overruns, and no zones of control.

The Highland Directorate's hover raiders come down out of the hills to
cut the Littoral Compact's convoys on the delta road and burn its
forward command post at Port Iver.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./saltmarsh (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.saltmarsh.json.  ./saltmarsh --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

